    "body": "Yeah I had to guess how to do this. This is what the loop look like in C++ that am going for here:\r\n```cpp\r\n  Element* element = ElementTraversal::Next(*this, this);\r\n  while (element) {\r\n    if (auto* html_element = DynamicTo<HTMLElement>(element)) {\r\n      if (DynamicTo<HTMLDialogElement>(html_element) ||\r\n          html_element->HasPopoverAttribute()) {\r\n        element = ElementTraversal::NextSkippingChildren(*element, this);\r\n        continue;\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n```\r\nI considered changing the loop from a for-each loop to a while loop like chromium has so I could more explicitly skip a bunch of descendants, but that got complicated too.\r\n\r\n> If you were trying to just skip these elements, I think the correct thing would be \"then continue\"?\r\n\r\nAwesome! I made this change, how does it look? If it makes the algorithm stop considering all the descendants of the descendant dialog or popover then thats perfect",
