    "body": "Ah, no, the version I suggested just skips the descendant dialogs and popovers, whereas it seems like your C++ code skips descendants of dialogs and popovers too. I'm unclear from the issue and PR description which is the intended behavior. Can you say more on why the C++ code chose to skip descendants of dialogs and popovers?\r\n\r\nIf you want to also skip descendants of dialogs and popovers, I guess you could change\r\n\r\n> If descendant is a [dialog](https://whatpr.org/html/9120/interactive-elements.html#the-dialog-element) element or descendant's [popover](https://whatpr.org/html/9120/popover.html#attr-popover) attribute is not in the [no popover state](https://whatpr.org/html/9120/popover.html#attr-popover-none-state), then continue\r\n\r\nto\r\n\r\n> If descendant has an inclusive ancestor that is a dialog element or whose popover attribute is not in the no popover state, then continue.\r\n\r\nI can't immediately think of something simpler, mainly because the spec doesn't have an equivalent of `NextSkippingChildren`. I guess you could do a full tree traversal (either recursive or iterative) using children instead of descendants, and then it'd be easy to skip the children of something?",
