    "body": "> I'm unclear from the issue and PR description which is the intended behavior. Can you say more on why the C++ code chose to skip descendants of dialogs and popovers?\r\n\r\nConsider the following:\r\n```html\r\n<div id=parentpopover popover=manual>\r\n  <button>button</button>\r\n  <div id=childpopover popover=manual autofocus>\r\n    <button autofocus>autofocus button</button>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<script>\r\nchildpopover.showPopover();\r\nparentpopover.showPopover();\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen we call `parentpopover.showPopover()`, `childpopover` and its descendants should not be considered for initial focus despite the autofocus attributes.\r\n\r\nAs for historical context, I'll get back to you on that.\r\n\r\n> If descendant has an inclusive ancestor that is a dialog element or whose popover attribute is not in the no popover state, then continue.\r\n\r\nThanks, I changed it to this text\r\n\r\n> I guess you could do a full tree traversal (either recursive or iterative) using children instead of descendants, and then it'd be easy to skip the children of something?\r\n\r\nYeah at first I thought I would have to rewrite the entire loop but I wasn't sure exactly how to do it easily. Is there another example somewhere of a loop like this?",
