    "body": "Ok, I have a new example:\r\n```html\r\n<div id=parentpopover popover=manual>\r\n  <div id=childpopover popover=manual autofocus>\r\n    <button autofocus>child autofocus button</button>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <button autofocus>parent autofocus button</button>\r\n</div>\r\n<script>\r\nchildpopover.showPopover();\r\nparentpopover.showPopover();\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\n\r\nEach of these popovers are their own context for autofocus, and they shouldn't consider nested contexts when looking elements to give initial focus. This is the same behavior for page load when looking for an autofocus element - dialog and popover elements are skipped.\r\n\r\nIn this example, \"parent autofocus button\" should get initial focus",
