    "body": "> Why does childpopover have an autofocus attribute, if you don't want to autofocus it?\r\n\r\nIt was just to illustrate the behavior that during the parent's initial focus steps, the child popover element doesn't mess with the initial focus even if it has the autofocus attribute.\r\n\r\n> Why are you showing the child before the parent? Does that even work? I thought the parent would still be display: none so you wouldn't see the child.\r\n\r\nYes, you can't see the child without the parent also being shown. It does work, and this is the only case where this PR changes the behavior: when there is already a showing popover or open dialog child element of the popover we are running initial focus for. If the child dialog or popover is not showing, then it will not be considered for autofocus because it is not being rendered.\r\n\r\nSee this WPT for more examples: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/e039dcf6cfee11e44da7959f9acae8dfc386584a/html/semantics/popovers/popover-focus-child-dialog.html\r\n\r\nDo you think this is a use case we should or shouldn't support?",
